#. Tag: title
#: journey.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smile!"
msgstr "Sorrí! (\"Smile!\")"

#. Tag: para
#: journey.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again, such a strange thing. What is this ;-) meant to be? Turn your head so "
"the left side of your screen is on top; got it? It's a smile with a wink? "
"This is a so-called emoticon; emoticons are an often-used possibility to "
"express emotions, one thing missing in conversation on the Usenet (but there "
"is a substitute, remember? ;-)"
msgstr ""
"Outra volta, algo estraño. Que se supón que significa ;-)? Xire a cabeza de "
"xeito que a parte esquerda da pantalla estea arriba; cólleo? É un sorriso "
"cun ollo piscado? É o que se chama unha emoticona; as emoticonas (de "
"\"emoción\" e \"icona\") son unha posibilidade frecuente para expresar "
"emocións, algo que falta cando se parola na Usenet (mais hai un substituto, "
"lembra? ;-)"

#. Tag: para
#: journey.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is very difficult to express emotions in email or news; your joking "
"comment appear to be very serious to the recipient and can lead to unmeant "
"reactions or conflicts (flames); so use emoticons to express your intention."
msgstr ""
"Resulta realmente difícil expresar emocións nas mensaxes de correo e nas "
"novas; un comentario de carallada parécelle serio ao destinatario e pode "
"provocar reaccións inesperadas ou conflitos (\"flames\"); por iso debería "
"empregar as emoticonas para expresar a súa intención."

#. Tag: para
#: journey.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lots of emoticons, which express a great variety of emotions; "
"the interpretation is easy if you turn your head and think of a face."
msgstr ""
"Existen moitas emoticonas que expresan unha grande variedade de emocións; a "
"interpretación é doada se xira a cabeza e pensa nunha cabeza."

#. Tag: title
#: journey.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "PLONK!"
msgstr "PLONK!"

#. Tag: para
#: journey.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This PLONK! looks like some comic-sound, does it not? And that is exactly "
"what it is used for. The one who reads it knows he was just added to the "
"killfile of a newsreader; normally this means the recipient of the PLONK! "
"annoyed the sender. The PLONK! is meant to play back the sound of the "
"recipients name hitting the ground in the <glossterm>killfile</glossterm>."
msgstr ""
"Este PLONK! parece un son cómico, non é? E é precisamente para o que se "
"emprega. Quen o lea sabe que o acaban de engadir ao ficheiro killfile dun "
"lector de novas; normalmente significa que o destinatario do PLONK! anoxou o "
"remitente. O sentido de PLONK! é reproducir o son do nome do destinatario a "
"golpea o chan no <glossterm>killfile</glossterm>."
